WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:02.659
- Please welcome Rebecca Romijn, y'all!

00:00:02.659 --> 00:00:07.043
(audience applaud and cheer)

00:00:07.043 --> 00:00:07.960
Oh my gosh,

00:00:09.353 --> 00:00:10.766
you look beautiful.

00:00:10.766 --> 00:00:11.766
- Thank you.

00:00:13.174 --> 00:00:14.446
- Hi, Rebecca!

00:00:14.446 --> 00:00:17.946
(music drowns out speech)

00:00:21.035 --> 00:00:22.020
- Come on down.

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:23.200
Would you like some wine?

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:24.250
Wait, you can do it.

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:25.083
- Oh my gosh.
- Yes,

00:00:25.083 --> 00:00:27.998
she's like, "Don't step on my role, girl."

00:00:27.998 --> 00:00:30.590
But, tell me about this...

00:00:30.590 --> 00:00:33.130
Rescue Dog Show is first
of all the coolest thing.

00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:33.963
We grew up...

00:00:33.963 --> 00:00:36.530
My mother could not turn an animal away.

00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:38.720
We had every animal in our house.

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:39.553
- We did too.

00:00:39.553 --> 00:00:41.120
My mom was actually a cat rescuer.

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:42.210
We grew up with cats.
- [Kelly] We did too.

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:43.043
- More than dogs.

00:00:43.043 --> 00:00:44.030
I didn't have a dog as a child.

00:00:44.030 --> 00:00:45.450
But my mom was a real activist

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:46.910
who rescued feral cats,

00:00:46.910 --> 00:00:49.180
and get them fixed and
then re-release them.

00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:50.360
But as a kid you're like,

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:52.818
why can't we just bring
all the animals home?

00:00:52.818 --> 00:00:54.626
(audience laughs)
Why can't we have them all?

00:00:54.626 --> 00:00:56.760
- And that's what I love
about this Rescue Dog Show,

00:00:56.760 --> 00:00:58.590
is it's not best in show,

00:00:58.590 --> 00:01:01.430
or the most beautiful put together dog.

00:01:01.430 --> 00:01:02.263
It's like...

00:01:02.263 --> 00:01:03.215
Those aren't the fun ones.

00:01:03.215 --> 00:01:04.048
Those aren't--

00:01:04.048 --> 00:01:06.410
- The American Rescue Dog Show

00:01:06.410 --> 00:01:07.850
celebrates that...

00:01:07.850 --> 00:01:10.660
They're not dogs that are
judged on their bloodline,

00:01:10.660 --> 00:01:11.550
or their breed,

00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:12.990
they're judged for their personality

00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:13.940
and their character

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:15.080
and their quirkiness.

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:15.913
Their...

00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:18.170
Special quirks.
- It's cute.

00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:19.730
Do you just wanna adopt all of them?

00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:21.450
I'm bad at that.
- Well all the dogs

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:24.170
on The American Rescue Dog Show
have already been spoken for

00:01:24.170 --> 00:01:25.830
which is why we say they're all winners

00:01:25.830 --> 00:01:28.290
because they've all found
their forever homes.

00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:30.490
But we're celebrating their uniqueness

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:34.190
and spreading the word about dog rescue

00:01:34.190 --> 00:01:36.350
and the categories are amazing.

00:01:36.350 --> 00:01:38.030
We have Best In Belly Rubs.

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:39.329
This year we have Best In Wrinkles.

00:01:39.329 --> 00:01:40.850
(laughs)

00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:42.250
Best In Ears.

00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:43.380
Best In Snoring,

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:45.660
which is always a crowd-pleaser.

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:47.750
Best In Couch Potato.

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:48.710
- Couch Potato is awesome.

00:01:48.710 --> 00:01:51.570
- And then the two that always make me cry

00:01:51.570 --> 00:01:52.850
are Best In Senior

00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:54.180
and Best In Special Needs.

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:56.400
- Wow, that's amazing.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:58.050
So speaking of loving your dogs,

00:01:58.050 --> 00:01:59.500
having them in your house all the time,

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:01.440
are y'all the kind of people that have...

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:03.843
Do you sleep with your
dogs in your bed, or no?

00:02:04.830 --> 00:02:05.714
- No.
- No.

00:02:05.714 --> 00:02:06.770
(audience laughs)

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:09.310
- I love animals,

00:02:09.310 --> 00:02:10.720
possibly more than humans,

00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:12.934
and I'm like, boo this is my bed, get out.

00:02:12.934 --> 00:02:16.000
- And you get to an age where
sleep becomes so precious--

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:16.833
- Whoa.

00:02:16.833 --> 00:02:18.510
- Nothing is gonna come
between me and that.

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:21.220
- And bed is for sleeping
or something else,

00:02:21.220 --> 00:02:22.110
and you're not involved.

00:02:22.110 --> 00:02:23.950
- That's right, that's right.

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:25.130
Beat it.

00:02:25.130 --> 00:02:25.963
Beat it.

00:02:25.963 --> 00:02:26.890
- So you don't either.

00:02:26.890 --> 00:02:29.630
- No, yeah, you wanna keep
your dog out of your bedroom.

00:02:29.630 --> 00:02:31.370
I think, I think that's a good call.

00:02:31.370 --> 00:02:33.862
Because however they react
won't be the right way.

00:02:33.862 --> 00:02:35.272
(laughing)

00:02:35.272 --> 00:02:36.760
- I love that everyone in the audience

00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:39.181
is thinking of the time in their life

00:02:39.181 --> 00:02:41.403
when that story has applied.

